From fa8f2382d10f6ce0e1960084734bf79e60bd9568 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev <dev@local>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:58:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] perf(render): cap canvas backing stores at 2x device
 pixels

A 3x phone was giving these canvases nine times the CSS-pixel area, and canvas
cost scales with pixels: nine times the fill, nine times the texture upload. The
visualizers that draw with motion, glow and blur cannot show the difference
between 2x and 3x, but the frame time doubles. lumiere already made this trade
(LUMIERE_MAX_RENDER_RESOLUTION = 2); this extends the same cap to the renderers
that missed it.

- src/utils/canvasPixelRatio: resolveCanvasPixelRatio clamps to 1..2, one place
  for the cap and one place to change it.
- cadenza's text canvas, monet's audio overlay, pendolo's clockwork canvas and
  fume's stage now size their backing store and setTransform from it. Both
  numbers come from the same helper on purpose: a backing store sized by one
  ratio and transformed by another stretches the picture.
